    <section class="ovation-extra-content ovation-serial-locations" aria-labelledby="ovation-serial-find-title">
      <h2 id="ovation-serial-find-title">How to find a serial number on an Ovation guitar</h2>

      <div class="ovation-serial-group">
        <h3>1. Inside the Sound Hole (Most Common)</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Paper or Foil Label:</strong> Look directly through the sound hole. Most Ovation guitars have a label toward the neck end of the bowl. The serial number is often printed on a small silver or white sticker located above the main model badge.</li>
          <li><strong>Neck Block:</strong> On some older USA-made models (roughly 1968 to 1972), the serial number may be stamped directly into the wood of the neck block inside the guitar.</li>
          <li><strong>Near the Heel:</strong> Check the area between the main inside label and the heel of the neck. Some owners report finding a small sticker in this specific location.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="ovation-serial-group">
        <h3>2. Exterior Locations</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Back of the Headstock:</strong> On certain models, particularly those made around 1995 or later, the serial number may be stamped or printed on the back of the headstock.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="ovation-serial-group">
        <h3>3. Tips for Locating It</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Use a Flashlight:</strong> Because the bowl is dark and the stickers can be small, shining a light inside the sound hole is often necessary to spot the number.</li>
          <li><strong>Check the Bottom of the Bowl:</strong> If the label is missing, it may have dried out and fallen off; check the very bottom of the guitar's interior to see if it is rolling around inside.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
